  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pathways for inclusive and gender responsive national policy instruments to eradicate hunger and poverty</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Dominican Republic and Sierra Leone have committed, through their participation in the Global Alliance Against Hunger and Poverty (GAAHP), to bring socio-economic inclusion to scale through evidence-based, large-scale policies and programmes that empower smallholder farmers and promote gender equality. This project aims at supporting the readiness of these countries to implement such commitments, in alignment with Global frameworks SDGs (SDG 1, 2, 5 among others).</narrative>
  </description>
